    "tip": "Excessive dry heat toughens meat, while moist heat tenderises it through collagen turning to gelatine; students often mix these up. For three effects of heat on protein foods, choose from coagulation, colour change, denaturation, more digestible, collagen to gelatine, softer meat, improved flavour and destroying micro-organisms."
